      "text": "Diamond and charcoal are the same stuff.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "hook"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "In 1772, Lavoisier burned a diamond with a lens that focused sunlight.",
      "say": "In seventeen seventy two, Lah vwah zyay burned a diamond with a lens that focused sunlight.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "real",
        "src": "359-diamond-and-charcoal-are-the-same-stuff-0.jpg",
        "fit": "card",
        "label": "Antoine Lavoisier",
        "credit": "Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The gas it gave off turned limewater cloudy.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "ring",
        "stone": "diamond",
        "cut": "round",
        "metal": "platinum",
        "halo": 10,
        "label": "Limewater turned cloudy"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Then English chemist Smithson Tennant took the puzzle further.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "real",
        "src": "359-diamond-and-charcoal-are-the-same-stuff-1.jpg",
        "fit": "card",
        "label": "Smithson Tennant",
        "credit": "Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "He used a gold tube, closed at one end.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "band",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "stone": "topaz",
        "label": "A gold tube"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "He heated two and a half grains of diamonds with niter.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "stone",
        "stone": "diamond",
        "cut": "cushion",
        "metal": "platinum",
        "label": "Two and a half grains"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "He kept it red hot for about an hour and a half.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Red hot",
        "sub": "An hour and a half",
        "piece": "ring",
        "stone": "ruby",
        "cut": "round",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "halo": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Only one gas came off: carbon dioxide.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "earrings",
        "stone": "diamond",
        "cut": "round",
        "metal": "platinum",
        "label": "Only carbon dioxide"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It was about what the same weight of charcoal gives.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "bracelet",
        "stone": "amethyst",
        "metal": "platinum",
        "label": "Like charcoal"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Tennant concluded a diamond is charcoal in crystal form.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "necklace",
        "stone": "diamond",
        "cut": "pear",
        "metal": "platinum",
        "label": "Charcoal in crystal form"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "His paper On the Nature of the Diamond came out in 1797.",
      "say": "His paper On the Nature of the Diamond came out in seventeen ninety seven.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
